Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 55 CLINICAL DATA  Thirty nine year old with breast carcinoma  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID b  Complete response to chemotherapy  Now for mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LEFT BREAST  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN DENSE FIBROUS SCAR TISSUE WITH CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  HEMOSIDERIN DEPOSITION  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTIONS TO SUTURE MATERIAL AND FAT NECROSIS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Resection margins are free of tumor  Metastatic carcinoma in 3 of 8 lymph nodes  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 56                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 54     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a 27 x 20 x 6cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 26 x 15cm overlying skin ellipse which contains a 3 5cm long scar in the outer quadrant  4cm lateral to the 5cm in diameter grossly unremarkable nipple  Cross sectioning of the scar reveals a 1 5cm in diameter ill defined  white fibrous tissue   2cm beneath the scar  with surrounding fat necrosis but no gross evidence of tumor  This scar tissue is at least 1 5cm from the closest inferior resection margin  A random section of this fibrous area is frozen as frozen section  1 and submitted in cassette A  The remainder of the breast consists of mostly of mature  yellow adipose tissue  which is intersected by scant  white  fibrous strands  No areas grossly suspicious of tumor are identified  The axillary tail measures 9 x 5 x 3cm and contains several tan  soft to rubbery lymph nodes  Section Code B F   cross sections through scar and entire remaining biopsy cavity G   nipple H Q   lymph nodes Resident  Sigrid Regauer  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , No.
