 uninvolved parenchyma is predominately tan yellow adipose tissue  Entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy site  entirely submitted  from anterior to posterior  with margins present in each section   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of tissue away from the mass  Gross Dictation by Julie Ann Nagle Warner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Julie Ann Nagle Warner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  Deeper levels were examined on the block   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the focus of ductal carcinoma in situ  In the deeper levels  the size of the focus of ductal carcinoma in situ increases to 0 25cm  the grade increases to grade 2 of 3  and the focus is closer to the margin  less than 0 05cm   Addendum  1 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Note  Although calcifications were not evident on the specimen radiograph  the tissue blocks were radiographed and minute calcifications noted in 1 block  Deeper levels performed on this block show focal microcalcifications associated with benign lobules in the region of the healing biopsy site  Addendum  3 by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on 