Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 17 54 CLINICAL DATA  47 year old woman with stage IIIB breast cancer  status post chemotherapy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MULTIFOCAL  SPANNING AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE   2  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 13 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   SEE TABLE  1   Note  All resection margins are greater than 0 2cm  Definite blood vascular invasion is not identified  The tumor is multifocal in nature and a definite overall size is difficult to assess  the residual invasive carcinoma most likely spans greater than 1 7cm  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES Number of positive lymph nodes  2 Number of lymph nodes examined  13 Number of lymph nodes with metastases less than 0 2cm  2 Size of largest lymph node  0 4cm Extracapsular extension  None Other forms of axillary involvement  None Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 12 27                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 07 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast and axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left mastectomy with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm nipple bearing skin ellipse is notable for a 1 0cm superior linear  well healed scar  Within the parenchyma and underlying the scar  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm centrally located firm fibrous area  This is located 2 5cm from the deep margin  6 5cm from the superior margin  6 5cm from the inferior margin  and abuts the skin  There is a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined area of fibrous thickening that is located 2 3cm inferior to the first area  It abuts the anterior inferior margin  is 1 5cm from the posterior inferior margin  and is 3 0cm from the inferior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  There is an unattached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular fragment of yellow adipose tissue that is grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A C  Representative sections of larger firm fibrous area  with skin in A  D  Closest posterior margin to larger mass  E F  Second smaller area of firm fibrosis with anterior margin  G  Second smaller area of firm fibrosis with posterior margin  H I  Representative sections of parenchyma away from fibrous areas  with ink representing posterior  J  Representative sections of separate piece of adipose tissue  Within the axillary tail multiple tan white lymph nodes are identified  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension  Whole lymph nodes are submitted in K through M and representative sections of individual lymph nodes are submitted in N  Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD                                                                                 S