Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 47 CLINICAL DATA  The patient has a right breast mass  now status post needle localization                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  65   AT THE INKED MARGIN OF RESECTION  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE  35   FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 46     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm excisional breast biopsy with localizing wire in place  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 5cm in diameter firm nodule  abutting the inked surface  and corresponding in position to the calcification near the thick segment of the localizing wire seen radiographically  A representative portion is frozen as frozen section  1  and kept frozen  The remainder of the tissue is submitted entirely in cassettes A through F  with the nodule in cassette A  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS , Not_reported.
