the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast tissue which is incised and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0 3cm area of firm white tan poorly defined tissue  which is too small to freeze  This area was adjacent to the wire corresponding to calcifications  The firm area is in cassettes A through D  The remainder is in cassettes E through I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm tan stellate area extending to margin  Tissue submitted entirely in J through M  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST LUMP   ONE FIVE MILLIMETER AREA OF INDURATION  TO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Armaghan A Mostafavi  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY  SPCIMEN  1   LUMP  PART B  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY  SPCIMEN  2   MASS    report_end  , No.
