00 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 06 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm oriented breast biopsy  The specimen is inked as follows  the medial half   black  lateral half   blue  posterior surface   green over blue or black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm in maximum diameter white gray firm stellate nodule abutting the posteromedial resection margin  A representative section of tumor with posteromedial margin is frozen as FX 1  now submitted in A  The tumor is entirely submitted in A D  Additional breast parenchyma is submitted in E H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   1   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  bisected and entirely submitted in I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   2  are two pieces of tan yellow fibroadipose breast tissue  each REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The pieces are submitted entirely in J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   3   are two pieces of tan yellow fibroadipose breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  respectively  Each is submitted in K and L  respectively  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA TO POSTERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnos