Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 06 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  MASS    RE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT  CAVITY    EXCISION  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  RARE FOCI  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  BREAST  LEFT   ADJACENT    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The lymph node does not contain keratin positive tumor cells  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 43                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of yellow white fibroadipose breast tissue  which is submitted entirely as FX 1 and resubmitted as Cassette A  Also received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number  and  left adjacent  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fibroadipose breast tissue with a tan stellate mass with fibrous extension  which is submitted entirely in Cassettes B E  Also received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy cavity   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose breast tissue  with suture marking edge farthest from the tumor  The specimen is inked black and the edge farthest from the tumor is over inked blue  The entire specimen is submitted in Cassettes F I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  submitted entirely in Cassettes J K  Resident  SAMANTHA J  PULLIAM  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  Dr  Prabha Pai O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                               