ing multiple blue dome cysts measuring 0 2cm in greatest dimension  This fibrous area is 3 0cm from the closest  deep  margin  1 0cm medial to this is an additional area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm which is rough white and irregular and is 1 5cm from the closest  deep  margin  these areas have been described from medial to lateral  The remainder of the specimen is composed of fibroadipose tissue and scattered blue dome cysts measuring up to 0 2cm  No discrete biopsy cavity is identified  Section codes  A  medial most hard nodule with posterior margin B C  remainder of above nodule D  fibrous areas surrounding nodule E F  second area mentioned in gross  fibrous nodule G  third nodule and posterior margin H  remainder of third nodule I  area of white cysts 2 0cm inferior to the second nodule J K  uninvolved medial tissue L  uninvolved lateral tissue From the attached axillary tail  multiple lymph nodes are identified measuring in size up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Representative sections of lymph nodes are submitted in R V  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional superficial margin  upper outer quadrant   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of yellow tan fibroadipose tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue which is entirely submitted in M O  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of yellow red fibroadipose tissue  from which multiple lymph nodes measuring up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm are identified and submitted as follows  Section code  P  representative sections of four lymph nodes Q  one lymph node entirely submitted Resident  SAMANTHA J  PULLIAM  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REP