Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 27 CLINICAL DATA  Carcinoma of the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 3  EXTENDING REMOVED_DATE CM FROM CLOSEST ANTERIOR MARGIN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  All resection margins are free of tumor  No definite lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT BREAST   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 3 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 01                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 18 x 17 x 1 5cm right simple mastectomy specimen  with an overlying 13 x 5 5cm skin ellipse with a centrally placed grossly unremarkable nipple  No surgical scars are identified on the skin ellipse  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm stellate hard  pink mass is present  approximately 2cm below the skin ellipse  1 5cm from the closest deep margin and 0 9cm from the closest anterior margin  The remaining parenchyma is composed of grossly unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Within the breast parenchyma  approximately three lymph nodes are identified  SECTION CODE A B  Representative sections of tumor  C