Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  21 MAY 98 at 13 37 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  SEVERAL NODULES  AGGREGATING TO APPROXIMATELY REMOVED_DATE CM  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVELY INVOLVING THE BREAST AND FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MEDIAL AND DEEP MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of invasive carcinoma  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 26 OF 26 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SEPARATELY SUBMITTED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 15 13                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a 