iochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are five parts  Labeled  right breast mass   is a 122 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  The external surface is grossly unremarkable and inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a central gray white  firm to rubbery  centrally cystic mass REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  extending to within 0 4cm of an inked margin  The remaining breast tissue are strands of white pink fibrous septae in unremarkable yellow fibroadipose tissue  No other suspicious nodules are identified in the specimen  Representative sections of the tumor with margin are submitted in cassettes A through I  Representative sections of breast tissue are submitted in cassettes J through O  Labeled  right axillary lymph nodes  level 2   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue containing several rubbery nodules  in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Representative tissue is submitted in cassettes P through R  Labeled  axillary lymph nodes  level 1   is a mass of adipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes and several detached lymph node fragments  the mass of fibroadipose tissue is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm and remaining aggregate of lymph nodes is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes S through W  Labeled  axillary lymph node  level 1   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a single fragment of fibroadipose tissue containing a lymph node  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  Specimen is bisected and submitted entirely in cassettes X and Y  Labeled  axillary lymph node  level 1  121   is a single pink tan  rubbery nodule REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette Z  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  Irene Kuter  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PARTIAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  LEVEL 2  EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  LEVEL 1  EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODE  LEVEL 1    REMOVED_CASE_ID   EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODE  LEVEL 1   121  EXCISION , No.
