Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 45 CLINICAL DATA  Right colectomy for colon cancer  right mastectomy for carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATE TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  97    REMOVED_DATE CM IN MAXIMUM DIMENSION  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURGICAL MARGINS   SEE NOTE   NOTE  No definite lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3    MULTIPLE SMALL FOCI  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 41 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IM