Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 30 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Neither vascular nor lymphatic invasion is identified  The in situ foci are situated in the main tumor mass  not apart from it  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    SOLID AND CRIBRIFORM TYPES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 54                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  NEGATIVE  progesterone receptor  NOT DETERMINED  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 32     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  EXCISIONAL   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   14   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 30     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm piece of unoriented firm to rubbery  pink  tan fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a stellate  gray white  hard lesion at one end  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm  grossly extending to inked margin  Representative sections are frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  Tissue is sent for estrogen receptor and BRDU studies  Representative sections of non frozen tissue are submitted in A through J  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  PRESENT GROSSLY AT MARGIN  O R  Re