tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 AUG 93 at 09 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm piece of breast parenchyma with two localizing wires and an x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to show a gray pink  hard stellate lesion 0 7cm in greatest diameter  There is a 0 2cm firm  gray pink lesion at the surgical margin  A representative section of thin area is frozen as frozen section  1  Frozen section  1 will be kept frozen  The remainder of the specimen will be submitted in cassettes  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  P  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D                                                          