ve value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 MAY 98 at 16 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  are two small fragments  the larger measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  and the smaller fragment measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The fragments of tissue are inked and serially sectioned to reveal dense white  cystic parenchyma with larger cysts noted in the larger fragment of tissue  The larger fragment is submitted entirely in cassettes A and B with the smaller fragment entirely in cassette C  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm breast fragment with a dense white cystic parenchyma  the largest cyst measuring 0 6cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes D   I  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   BOTH FRAGMENTS NOT SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1 PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  2   report_end  , No.
